    {
      "heading": "Reading rules",
      "text": [
        "Stress: every Russian word has one stressed syllable, and it can fall anywhere. Ordinary Russian text doesn't mark it, so the IPA in this app always shows it with ˈ.",
        "Unstressed vowels weaken: о is only [o] when stressed — elsewhere it sounds like a (молоко [məɫɐˈko]). Unstressed е and я sound like a short i (сестра [sʲɪˈstra]).",
        "Voiced consonants at the end of a word lose their voice: хлеб sounds like [xlʲep], друг like [druk]."
      ]
    },
